concepts.content:
To apply a convolutional layer to a multichannel image, such as an RGB image $\mathbf{x}_{\texttt{in}}\in \mathbb{R}^{3 \times N \times M}$, we use a multichannel filter $\mathbf{w} \in \mathbb{R}^{C \times K \times K}$. We filter each input channel with the corresponding filter channel and then sum the responses:
$$\begin{aligned}    \mathbf{x}_{\texttt{out}}= \sum_{c} \mathbf{w}[c,:,:] \star \mathbf{x}_{\texttt{in}}[c,:,:] + b[c] & \quad \triangleleft \quad\texttt{conv}\quad \text{(multichannel in)}
\end{aligned}$$

